{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385328-v5-houserule-hecata-bane-and-disciplines","id":1385328,"title":"[V5] Houserule: Hecata Bane and Disciplines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-02T17:28:38-07:00","id":1385328,"title":"[V5] Houserule: Hecata Bane and Disciplines","content":"I've never really liked the V5 Hecata bane's mechanics, especially the way it's spreading to all necromancers post-Reunion. So here's my alternative take.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Bane: </b>The Hecata have spent centuries studying the mysteries of death and undeath, and this morbidity has infected their blood. While Lasombra see Oblivion affecting technology around them, the Hecata are cursed in a more subtle way: they are affected by wards, exorcisms, abjurations, and other ceremonies as if they were ghosts.<br /> <br /> Blood Sorcery rituals and Oblivion ceremonies like the </i>Warding Circle Against Spirits <i>affect them thoroughly and completely, following the usual rules for such wards. But simpler defenses can be discovered and performed by any mortal with enough time and Occult knowledge: anything from a salt circle sealed with a drop of blood to reciting the Exorcism of Saint Benedict in a particular dialect of Latin might offer protection against wraiths. A Hecata who wants to cross such a ward, affect a protected individual, or stay within line of sight of an exorcism must spend willpower equal to their Bane Severity per scene.</i><br /> <br /> The painful bite still makes sense for Lamiae and Giovanni, of course, so:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Feeding Flaw: Lamia\u2019s Bite (\u2022\u2022):</b> Your fangs do not cause the rush of pleasure and blurred memory of the Kiss. Instead, when you bite a mortal, they\u2019re aware of exactly what\u2019s happening\u2014and feel exactly as much pain as one might expect from half-inch fangs being forced into their neck. This does not cause any additional damage, but makes it difficult to maintain a Herd, and can pose serious difficulties for the Masquerade.</i><br /> <br /> In my headcanon, all the necromantic bloodlines have <u>always</u> had this affected-by-wards bane, which according to legend was passed down from Cappadocius himself. Over time, different bloodlines developed different banes on top of this, which are represented as two-point Flaws (<i>Obvious Predator</i>, <i>Repulsive</i>, <i>Lamia's Bite</i>) passed down from Sire to childe. Post-Reunion, some Hecata from different bloodlines have found ways to mix their blood to create a childe who has no bloodline bane, only the clan bane: these are the new &quot;baseline&quot; Hecata, for players who want to spend their chargen flaw points on something else.<br /> <br /> I also houserule away the need for Auspex to compel ghosts (so the Giovanni can keep their Dominate), but as an alternative, for people who want to keep the RAW power requirements:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Merit: Versatile Blood (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> The changes in the Blood that have happened since the Family Reunion are still not well understood. Your Blood is a particular mystery: it\u2019s adapted more easily than many others\u2019, while still retaining some of the power of your pre-Hecata ancestors. You have four in-clan disciplines: Auspex, Fortitude, Oblivion, and any one of Dominate, Obfuscate, or Potence (depending on your lineage).</i><br /> <br /> I'd still let Giovanni choose between Auspex and Dominate without buying this merit, but the merit lets them get both, to keep consistent with both their old flavor and their current mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T01:15:25-07:00","id":1385375,"title":"","content":"Isn't Hecata supposed to be a sect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T05:59:43-07:00","id":1385394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385328-v5-houserule-hecata-bane-and-disciplines?p=1385375#post1385375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Hecata supposed to be a sect?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are independent, as it was the Clan Giovanni. They could be considered a sect, but probably they lack the hierarchies, structure and titles that the Camarilla, Anarchs and Sabbat have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T10:54:15-07:00","id":1385432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385328-v5-houserule-hecata-bane-and-disciplines?p=1385375#post1385375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Hecata supposed to be a sect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. Like how members of any clan can convert and join the Church of Set, and conversely not all the vampires with snake powers care about Set.<br /> <br /> At this point &quot;Hecata&quot; means both &quot;necromantic vampires descended from Cappadocius&quot; and &quot;a particular alliance of bloodlines led by the Giovanni family&quot;, even though the two don't fully overlap (there are people in the alliance with no blood descent from Cappadocius, and people descended from Cappadocius with no interest in the alliance). It's a bit awkward, but it's what we've got; I personally use &quot;Hecata&quot; for the clan and &quot;Hecata Alliance&quot; for the sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}